workedExamples.question_text:
A triangular prism has the right-triangle cross-section shown and is $8$ cm long. Find its volume in cm³.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=4mm,y=4mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(6,0)--(0,2.5)--cycle;
\draw (0.35,0)--(0.35,0.35)--(0,0.35);
\path (3,0) node[below] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,1.25) node[left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (3,1.25) node[above right] {$13\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A prism has the parallelogram cross-section shown and is $9$ m long. Find its volume in m³.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(6,0)--(7.5,3)--(1.5,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (1.5,3)--(1.5,0);
\draw (1.5,0.3)--(1.8,0.3)--(1.8,0);
\path (3,0) node[below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\path (1.5,1.5) node[right] {$4\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A swimming pool is $18.6$ m long and $6.4$ m wide. Its floor slopes evenly from $1.35$ m deep to $2.75$ m deep. The side-wall cross-section is shown. Find the full volume of water in m³, correct to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,-1.35)--(6,-2.75)--(6,0)--cycle;
\path (3,0) node[above] {$18.6\text{ m}$};
\path (0,-0.675) node[left] {$1.35\text{ m}$};
\path (6,-1.375) node[right] {$2.75\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

